    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0177" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/7–747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grady</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-07T09:00:00+05:30">July 7, 1947—9 a.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>491. I shall issue following statement at press conference today: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have no instructions from my Government but speaking for myself I can
                            see no reason why, on the establishment of the two Dominions, there
                            should not be prompt recognition of the fact by Washington. As to
                            diplomatic representation, I would point out that all the Dominions are
                            represented in Washington and, similarly, we have representation in all
                            the Dominions.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Any attempt to evade or escape this issue would only arouse ill-feeling and give
                    rise to distorted reports re diplomatic recognition Pakistan.</p>
                <p>It would be helpful to our future relations with Pakistan if the Secretary would
                    at a press conference confirm and possibly elaborate my statement. I have
                    avoided use of word Pakistan.</p>
                <p>Trevelyan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d102-f1"/> had told Donovan<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d102-f2"/> Pakistan plan have Embassy Washington but no indication
                    who will fill post.</p>
                <p>Sysons, Deputy High Commissioner, says quarters for five Embassies reserved
                    Karachi: Great Britain, USA, France and “Malaya” and “Arab States.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grady</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d102-f1" n="1" xml:id="d102-f1-content">
                <p>Humphrey Trevelyan, predecessor of Major M. O. Ali Baig as First Secretary to the
                    Agent General for India.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d102-f2" n="2" xml:id="d102-f2-content">
                <p>Howard Donovan, Counselor of Embassy at New Delhi.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
